$image_clip — slideshow video with audio track

SUMMARY
  Builds one MP4 per sound in sounds[]: still images from images[] are shown
  as a slideshow whose total length matches the audio duration, then the
  audio is muxed in with moviepy.

SYNTAX
  $image_clip
  $image_clip(fps=25)

INPUT
  images[] — required; PNG/JPEG paths used as slides.
  sounds[] — required; WAV/MP3/etc. duration sets slideshow length.

OUTPUT
  videos[] — one MP4 per sound file ({timestamp}_image_clip_{i}.mp4).

ARGUMENTS
  fps= — frames per second for the silent slideshow (default 25).

BEHAVIOR
  1) ffprobe — audio duration
  2) duration / N images → seconds per slide; × fps → frames per image
  3) ffmpeg — PNG sequence → silent H.264 MP4
  4) moviepy — mux audio + video → final file

REQUIREMENTS
  ffmpeg and ffprobe on PATH; moviepy (included in media venv / uv sync --extra media).

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_IMAGE_CLIP=1 — write stub .mp4 text files without ffmpeg.

EXAMPLE
  @gen_clip: (@clip_images, @track) -> $image_clip -> $save('output.mp4')

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No.
